    "Aula de Ciencia: booking markup explicitly shows 24, 28, 29 and 30 December 2026. EUR 40 each or EUR 135 for all 4; two children EUR 80 / EUR 270 before optional care. Venue FAQ says Spanish and Valencian with the language adapted by group. The actual session language is conditional.",
    "Aula de Ciencia FIRST Explore: both children fit the published 6–9 range if already age 6 at entry. The Explore group is marked full. No official tournament date or direct entry is implied.",
    "ROBBO Poblenou: 33 published Saturday dates, 27 future dates after the check day. Parallel ages 6–9, 9–11, 12–15. Minimum enrollment and workshop language unconfirmed; Spanish/Russian only evidenced for the earlier open day. EUR 30 one workshop or EUR 100 for four consecutive published dates. The 3D sessions are linked pairs.",
    "Graellsia: day and residential alternatives in the same nature and science programme, EUR 150 without meals and EUR 260 full-board. Posted sibling discount 10%. Published age and school stages both remain visible. The overnight variant is a continuous stay and does not use day-only departure times.",
    "TechLab Kids Barcelona: Christmas choices and TBKids Christmas already exist with stable IDs. New 2027 Semana Blanca, Semana Santa and summer windows have closed registration and no added exact days. EISB Chess and Science continue to show July 2027 alongside 2026 fees. The EISB English science track is distinct from robotics.",
    "Madrid es Ciencia: official 2027 educator rules specify La Nave Madrid, 11–13 March, 10:00–19:00. The extended school project deadline is 16 November. January 2027 refers to organized school visits; individual family tickets and age conditions are still unconfirmed.",
    "Codi Cup: grades 5–6 at Catalan schools, 2–3 per team. School application, project submission, selection and awards have separate dates. Rules in Catalan alone do not establish the language requirement.",
    "ASTI: official current schedule specifies four March 2027 semifinals without days. Corrected the stable Burgos card and added four month-only route records. Both children are below the competition school level.",
    "MUNCYT: Misión Laboratorio is for ages 6–9 and is undated until a booking is available. The robotics lecture is family-marked but its content is secondary level. The Coruña Game Jam introduction is a workshop, with a strict 14–30 age range and an own-computer requirement."
